        -:   52:/**
        -:   53: * A subgraph is a set of items that are electrically connected on a single sheet.
        -:   54: *
        -:   55: * For example, a label connected to a wire and so on.
        -:   56: * A net is composed of one or more subgraphs.
        -:   57: *
        -:   58: * A set of items that appears to be physically connected may actually be more
        -:   59: * than one subgraph, because some items don't connect electrically.
        -:   60: *
        -:   61: * For example, multiple bus wires can come together at a junction but have
        -:   62: * different labels on each branch.  Each label+wire branch is its own subgraph.
        -:   63: */
